  "status": "published",
  "description_nl": "One row per model: provider (a providers.settings id), kind (text / image / video), id (what the provider calls it), label, and its price - text: in / out USD per million tokens; image: usd_per_image and size; video: usd_per_second_low / high, the clip lengths it makes (seconds), needs_image (Runway makes video FROM a picture: the storyboard still or the chain's last frame), ratios per aspect. fal.ai rows (2026-09-20, the cheap road): id = the text-to-video endpoint, image_id = the image-to-video one (used when a shot has a first frame), fields = what each model CALLS the prompt / image / duration / aspect / negative / resolution ('' = the model has no such field, nothing is sent), duration_text = the seconds go as text ('5'), aspect_from_image = no aspect is sent with a picture (the picture decides), resolution = the fixed value sent, video_path = where the file's URL sits in the answer. Google's own models stay in store.models / board.settings / film.settings. Prices are what the providers publish today (2026-09; the fal.ai ones are approximate) - edit them when they change; an unpriced model shows as unknown, never $0.",
